{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Problems and Solutions", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Staying Afloat", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 3, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 12, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.3", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Describe the reasons or results of events or actions in spoken or written texts, in work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn11le12ob03re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " The Present Perfect: Commenting on the Present Results of Something In the Past", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " You use the Present Perfect to talk about past actions that have a connection to the present.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "When you want to comment on the present results of a past action you can use the Present Perfect with verbs like <span class=\"italic\">appear, seem and sound.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">It <span class=\"strong\">sounds</span> as if <span class=\"strong\">you've already decided </span>on the next course of action.<br>It <span class=\"strong\">seems</span> they <span class=\"strong\">have completed </span>the report ahead of schedule.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The form of the Present Perfect is:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "subject + has/have + past participle", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You can use some typical expressions with the Present Perfect like<span class=\"italic\"> just, recently, already, lately, before, so far</span> etc.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I've invited Kristi as well, as it sounds as if she has some contacts in the media.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I want a tidal wave of publicity, which is why we have already come up with an exhaustive game plan for promotion. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I've already had our team come up with a logo.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I have always wanted to see Winnie brought to life, and now it seems as though you have already made it happen.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Report Verbs and the Agent of Verbs of Reporting", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use two patterns with report verbs: active and passive. <br>You use the passive when there is no reason to mention the agent (or doer) of the action.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "In some cases, you can choose to express the agent, but it is still seen as of secondary importance after the subject. Sometimes using the agent helps to clarify the source of the information for the reader or listener.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">It was mentioned <span class=\"strong\">by the director </span>that a few time slots might need to be filled, particularly in the morning.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Some common report verbs are:<span class=\"italic\"> claim, mention, request and point out.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Take a look at some examples of the passive construction of report verbs:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "It was claimed that BFP was the best, but I'm now I'm really beginning to see why.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "It was pointed out that Winnie is a tech-savvy hedgehog, so wouldn't it make sense for her to have her own twitter account?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "It was mentioned by the director that a few time slots might need to be filled, particularly in the morning.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "An interview was requested, but we're waiting to hear back about the exact time.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "buzz ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "excitement surrounding a product or event", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I know how important it can be to generate a little buzz. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le12ob03aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you use to discuss a publicity campaign.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "exhaustive ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "complete; including everything", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I want a tidal wave of publicity, which is why we have come up with an exhaustive game plan for promotion. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le12ob03aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "game plan", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a plan for achieving success", "type": "definition"}, {"content": " (noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Our game plan includes TV and radio.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le12ob03aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "leave no stone unturned ", "type": "name"}, {"content": " to do everything possible", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: No stone is left unturned when BFP works on a project.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le12ob03aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to exceed expectations ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to do more than expected", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We really try to exceed expectations.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le12ob03aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "tech-savvy ", "type": "name"}, {"content": " knowing a lot about technology", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It was pointed out that Winnie is a tech-savvy hedgehog, so wouldn't it make sense for her to have her own twitter account?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le12ob03aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "demographic ", "type": "name"}, {"content": " a group of people who are similar in certain characteristics like age or gender", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: That allows us to hit our target demographic, parents and kids, while they are eating breakfast.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le12ob03aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to air ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to broadcast something on radio or TV", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It will air Saturday morning, but the taping will probably occur sometime Friday afternoon.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le12ob03aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "diligence", "type": "name"}, {"content": "careful and persistent work", "type": "definition"}, {"content": " (noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: As always, thank you for your diligence. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le12ob03aud09", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Imagine that you have to promote a new book.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write a plan for a TV commercial to promote the book.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "\u201cPitch\u201d your TV commercial by presenting it to a partner.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I plan how to promote a book.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write an outline for a TV commercial.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I present my plan to a partner.", "type": "text"}]}], "labs": [{"id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type":